# Table §cell — THE ROW FORM TAKES NO PRESENTATION KEYS.
#
# `cell <r> highlight` tints a data row in the fixed highlight colour. Until
# 0.5 a `fill=`, `stroke=` or `class=` written on that line parsed,
# never reached the model, and drew nothing: a key silently discarded, the
# `ROW-HIGHLIGHT-CELL-FILL-COLLISION` defect class. Lines 17-19 pin the line error; line 20 pins that the
# bare row form is still legal.
figdown 0.5 table
class warn "a value outside its range"
table t "T"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| a1 | b1 |
| a2 | b2 |
| a3 | b3 |
| a4 | b4 |
cell 1 highlight fill=#ff0000
cell 2 highlight stroke=#ff0000
cell 3 highlight class=warn
cell 4 highlight
